# Exclude everything by default, then allowlist what the Dockerfile copies.
# Local test and type-check caches (__pycache__/, .mypy_cache/) would otherwise
# change the CDK image asset's hash between a working checkout and a clean
# clone of the same commit. Docker always reads the Dockerfile, and CDK keeps
# the Dockerfile and this file in the asset fingerprint.
*
!requirements.txt
!handler.py
